-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/2f47fd50-ab7c-5df0-99b3-1024f2f6945b
-- title:
--   Transfer of the blow-up chart C[J/a] to the Drinfeld chart
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Fixed are a prime $q$ with $5\le q$, a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero; an element $\xi\in L$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; and the hypothesis `hι` that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carries $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   **The function field and the base ring.** $K$ is an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ over $L$, and `hK` asserts $K=$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. $K$ is generated over $L$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ by the coefficientwise images (under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81)) of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H$ for $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Further, $A$ is a discrete valuation ring which is a Henselian local domain with algebraically closed residue field and with $L$ as fraction field, such that $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$. The element $j\in K$ is nonzero and its Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of the modular function $j$. Throughout, `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` denotes the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A ↥K j` is $j$ viewed in it. Finally $\varpi$ is a uniformiser of $A$ ($\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$, `hϖ`) and $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **The supersingular point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and `hss` requires: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The rigidity hypothesis `hArig`.** Let $X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the spectra of the two chart algebras along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$, and `ιFin` the morphism from `XFin` $=\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra. The hypothesis `hArig` quantifies over a point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` (`hϖz`) which is assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), and a point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin`$(y')=z$ whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as `hss`; for every such datum it asserts the existence of a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ (a domain, $\mathfrak m_W$-adically complete), a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f-$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $=f-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e:\ \widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}\ \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\ S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v-f\,u\bigr)$$
--   from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk, such that the following seven conditions hold, where $\mathrm{toC}$ is the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ the canonical ring homomorphism from the finite chart algebra to the stalk at $z$ (the germ along the image of `ιFin`, precomposed with the inverses of the `appIso` and $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ comparison isomorphisms):
--
--   (i) for all $a\in A$, $e$ carries the image of $a$ in the completed stalk to the class of $C(\sigma a)$;
--
--   (ii) for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — the condition that on quotients $f/g$ of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions, $\tau$ implements the action of $\gamma^{-1}$ through the matrix `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` under the complex embedding normalised by $\xi\mapsto\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$ — the automorphism $\tau$ preserves the finite chart algebra;
--
--   (iii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and such $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra, the induced endomorphism is the identity modulo $y'$;
--
--   (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra and acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ conjugates $e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ into the same map precomposed with $\tau$; $\theta$ fixes all constants $C(w)$; $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$; $c\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$; and $c\not\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$;
--
--   (v) separation of tangent directions: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct;
--
--   (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as in (v) whose tangent direction may be taken to be $(1,0)$, an element $a$ of the finite chart algebra has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$;
--
--   (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $q$-expansion of $j$ in the variable of level $q\ell$) lies in $K$ and in the finite chart algebra, is congruent modulo $y'$ to some $a_0\in A$, and the image of the difference under $e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ is the class of a power series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ for some $e_0\ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ part is nondegenerate in the sense that $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\bigl(\text{coefficient of }X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}\text{ in }h\bigr)a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ with at least one of $a,b$ outside $\mathfrak m_W$ and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   **The chosen presentation.** In addition to `hArig`, concrete data are given: a point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ with `hϖz`, `hz`, a point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin`$(y')=z$, the supersingularity `hss'` at $y'$, and `hy'y` : $y'$ corresponds to $y$; together with one presentation $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ as above (so $u_1,v_1$ units, $f_1\equiv$ `drinfeldForm q W₁` mod $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$) and the hypothesis `hW₁`, which is exactly the conjunction of the seven conditions (i)–(vii) for $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$ and $e_1$.
--
--   **The centre, the blow-up and the valuation ring.** `hJ` defines the ideal $J$ of the finite chart algebra as the infimum of all ideals of the form
--   $$\tau^{-1}\Bigl(\bigl(e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}\bigr)^{-1}\bigl(\,(\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\ \mathrm{mkS}\,X_0,\ \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1)\,\bigr)\Bigr),$$
--    taken over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the above sense which preserve the chart algebra. `hB` defines $B$ as the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained from the finite chart algebra by adjoining all $x\in K$ with $x\varpi_t\in J$ (that is, $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$ for $C$ the finite chart algebra). $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ with $B\subseteq W$ (`hBW`).
--
--   Four groups of hypotheses constrain $B$ and $W$. `hR1` (two clauses): $C\le B$, and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq0$. `hR2` (three clauses): $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of the finite chart algebra lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$; and $f\in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses): first, for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q κ` $-1$) whose kernel consists of the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, which is compatible with $A\to\kappa$, and which is equivariant in the sense that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $W$ stable under $\tau$ there is $c\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,c)\mapsto\det(g)\,c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho\circ\tau=$ `hAction q κ` of that pair, applied to $\rho$, with $c\neq1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; second, $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; third, every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ arises from some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense that $\tau$ maps the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ into $Q$; fourth, an element of $B$ whose images under all such $\tau$ lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by the image of $\varpi$; fifth, a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ on the chart algebra preserves $W$.
--
--   **The chosen centre element.** Finally $a$ is an element of the finite chart algebra with $a\in J$ and $a\neq0$ in $K$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, let $S$, $\mathrm{mkS}$, $\mathrm{toC}$ and $\mathrm{germY}$ be as above for the presentation $W_1,e_1$, and set
--   $$B_a:=C\bigl[\{x\in K:\ \exists\,i\in J,\ x\,a=i\}\bigr]\subseteq K\quad(\text{an }A\text{-subalgebra}),\qquad \Psi:=e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}:C\to S,$$
--   $s:=\Psi(a)$, $S[1/s]:=$ `Localization.Away s` with structure map $\iota:S\to S[1/s]$,
--   $$I:=\bigl(\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\ \mathrm{mkS}\,X_0,\ \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1\bigr),\qquad \mathfrak M:=\bigl(\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi),\ \mathrm{mkS}\,X_0,\ \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1\bigr),$$
--   and let $R$ be the $S$-subalgebra of $S[1/s]$ generated by all $w$ with $w\,\iota(s)=\iota(i)$ for some $i\in I$ (the affine blow-up algebra $S[I/s]$). Then there exists a ring homomorphism $\Phi:B_a\to S[1/s]$ such that:
--
--   1. $\Phi$ extends $\iota\circ\Psi$: for every $c\in C$ whose image in $K$ lies in $B_a$, $\Phi(c)=\iota(\Psi(c))$;
--
--   2. $\Phi$ divides as expected: for every $x\in B_a$ and every $i\in C$ with $i\in J$ and $x\,a=i$ in $K$, one has $\Phi(x)\,\iota(s)=\iota(\Psi(i))$;
--
--   3. $s$ is a non-zero-divisor of $S$;
--
--   4. $\Phi(B_a)\subseteq R$;
--
--   5. (exceptional fibre) for every $b\in B_a$: if $\Phi(b)$ can be written as
--   $$\Phi(b)=\bigl(\iota(\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))\cdot s^{-1}\bigr)\,r+\sum_{k<n}\iota(m_k)\,r'_k$$
--   with $r,r'_k\in R$ and $m_k\in\mathfrak M$ (finitely many, indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$, where $s^{-1}$ is `IsLocalization.Away.invSelf s`), then there exist $b'\in B_a$, a natural number $n$, elements $c_k\in C$ with $c_k\in y$ and elements $b''_k\in B_a$ such that, in $K$,
--   $$b=\varpi_t\,a^{-1}\,b'+\sum_{k<n}c_k\,b''_k.$$
--
--   The blow-up algebra occurring in the conclusion is the one with centre divided by $a$, whereas the algebra $B$ constrained by `hR1`–`hEQ` is the one with centre divided by $\varpi_t$.
--
--   This is the transfer step which compares the blow-up $C[J/a]$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra $C$ along the weighted centre $J$ with the affine blow-up $S[I/s]$ of the completed Drinfeld chart $S$ at the supersingular point $y$: it produces the comparison homomorphism $\Phi$ together with the statement that an element of $C[J/a]$ lying, after transfer, in the exceptional part $(\sigma_1\varpi_t/s)R+\mathfrak M R$ already lies in $(\varpi_t/a)B_a+yB_a$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_monic_aeval_div_eq_of_mem_centre_blowupChart_supersingular_fibre_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_monic_aeval_div_eq_of_mem_centre_blowupChart_supersingular_fibre_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), in the local analysis of the reduction of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ at a supersingular point.
